<title>NEW ZEALAND: Southland Building cuts NZ fixed rates.</title>
<headline>Southland Building cuts NZ fixed rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Southland Building Society said on Wednesday it had cut its one and two year fixed home loan lending rates to 8.8 percent and 9.05 percent respectively from the previous rate of 9.5 percent.  </p>
<p>The society with assets of $600 million said it was experiencing strong growth in lending.</p>
<p>It offers a variable lending rate of 9.75 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
